-- the arrangement at a tetrahedral atom: the cyclic order of three of its neighbours seen from the
-- fourth. The points are the triples and the paths are the three-cycles, so two arrangements are equal
-- exactly when they are rotations of one another — which is what a tetrahedral configuration is, and
-- an automorphism of a molecule with configurations must carry each arrangement to the same element.
data Cyc (A : Type 0) = cyc (a : A) (b : A) (c : A) | cyc-rot (a : A) (b : A) (c : A) (i : I) [ i = 0 ↦ cyc a b c , i = 1 ↦ cyc b c a ]
